1. Exact model: letters, P<=2, cells; cross-check with records_independent.py and symmetry.py
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
letters: 8 at a qutrit, 3 at a qubit (15 at d = 4, for Thm 2); structure constants exact and checked
P<=2 (at most two letters): dim 192 = 1 + 22 + 169
cells (class, exchange parity) and their dimensions, the same in every frame:
  id+:1, Q+:8, Q-:8, q+:3, q-:3, QQ+:36, QQ-:28, qq+:6, qq-:3, mS+:24, mS-:24, mC+:24, mC-:24
  (id identity; Q, q single letter at a qutrit copy / read qubit; QQ, qq, mS same-link mixed, mC cross mixed)
cross-check (records_independent.py and symmetry.py, imported unmodified; numerical rank tests, tol 1e-8):
  R_E = span of the Letter's 172 records; R_E' = span of the 172 covariant records of F-CT-10; their
  single-qubit parts are the Letter's three commutator records and symmetry.py's D_x, D_z, S_y.

2. Record spaces R_f = P2 + (f-odd single-qubit operators); C_L, C, C+; matchings
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C_L = E-odd single-qubit = span of the Letter's [s_mu,s_nu]_q1 - [s_mu,s_nu]_q2;  C = E'-odd;  C+ = E'-even:
  dim(C_L cap C) = 2
  dim(C_L cap C+) = 1
  dim(C cap C+) = 0
Lie(G_Omega) = E'-odd single-letter operators (8 at the join Q1Q2, 3 at the qubit pair q1q2); C is its qubit
  part.  Plain frame: dim(C_L cap Lie) = 2 (the x and z differences), dim(C_L+ cap Lie) = 1 (the y sum).
  R_f, f = E (plain; Letter, Lean) : classes (79, 48, 42, 3), numerator 79+48r2+42r3+3r6, 1/value 137.035999
  R_f, f = E' = E o T (F-CT-10)    : classes (79, 48, 42, 3), numerator 79+48r2+42r3+3r6, 1/value 137.035999
  R_f, f = Fm = (-1)^Nq E'         : classes (79, 48, 42, 3), numerator 79+48r2+42r3+3r6, 1/value 137.035999
  R_f, f = (-1)^NQ E'              : classes (79, 48, 42, 3), numerator 79+48r2+42r3+3r6, 1/value 137.035999
  R_f, f = sigma E' = (-1)^N E'    : classes (79, 48, 42, 3), numerator 79+48r2+42r3+3r6, 1/value 137.035999
  R_E = P2 + C_L,  R_E' = R_(-1)^NQ E' = P2 + C,  R_Fm = R_sigma E' = P2 + C+: three distinct spaces, same value

3. Order-definite composites (Thm 2); anticommuting letters at the qutrit (Prop. 3)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
at one end of dimension d: dim m(Sym^2 V), dim m(Lambda^2 V), dim of the intersection, dim traceless part of m(Sym^2 V)
  d = 2:  1,  3,  0,  0
  d = 3:  9,  8,  8,  8
  d = 4: 16, 15, 15, 15
m(V(x)V) = P<=2 (192); m(Sym^2 V) = 1 + P2 + V_Q1 + V_Q2 (186); m(Lambda^2 V) = the 22 single letters;
A = m(Sym^2 V) cap m(Lambda^2 V) = V_Q1 + V_Q2 (16).  The reversal of the two insertions descends to
m(V(x)V)/A; with the trace pairing, D = A^perp = 1 + P2 + V_q1 + V_q2 (176), D_+ = 1 + P2, D_- = V_q1 + V_q2,
and on D the order sign equals the own sign (-1)^N.  D_0 = D cap 1^perp = P2 + V_q1 + V_q2 (175).
one letter per read: QQ + qq + cross-mixed (121); both letters from one read: 1 + singles + same-link mixed (71)
  Gell-Mann (the Letter's letters)    : 5 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 4; pairs [(1, 2), (1, 3), (2, 3), (4, 5), (6, 7)]
  Lean real basis, d = 3              : 5 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 4
  Weyl X^a Z^b, d = 3                 : 0 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 0
  generic rational orthogonal, d = 3  : 0 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 0
  Pauli                               : 3 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 3
  Lean real basis, d = 2              : 3 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 3
  Weyl X^a Z^b, d = 2                 : 3 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 3
  generic rational orthogonal, d = 2  : 3 anticommuting pairs, their commutators span dim 3
  lambda_1..lambda_7 are singular (det 0), lambda_8 is not; the five anticommuting pairs' commutators span
  {lambda_1, lambda_2, lambda_3, lambda_8}.  The det argument of alpha.tex:109 excludes invertible reads only.

