  of the 2^11 sums of isotypic components, exactly one has dim 172: all but (10,1)_- and (10b,1)_- (it keeps
  the identity and all 22 single letters and drops 20 odd QQ records).  R_E' meets (8,1)_- (dim 16) in dim 8,
  (8,1)_+ in 8 and (1,1)_+ in 2 of 3: it is not a sum of isotypic components.
  R_Fm under SU(3) x SU(2) x <Fm> has the same isotypic table as R_E' under <E'> (F-CT-10 item 4): (1,1)_+ 2, (1,5)_+ 5, (27,1)_+ 27, (8,1)_+ 8, (8,3)_+ 48, (1,3)_- 6, (10+10b,1)_- 20, (8,1)_- 8, (8,3)_- 48

5. Identification rules (Thm 6); the covariant exchanges (Thm 7)
----------------------------------------------------------------
I = image of the identification algebras of the two read links = P<=1 (identity + 22 single letters, dim 23).
stab_Omega = {X in I : X|Omega> in C|Omega>} = 1 + Lie(G_Omega) (dim 12).
Comp_f = {X in I : f ad_X f = ad_X}:  Comp_E = I^E (the E-even part, 12);  Comp_f = stab_Omega for each of the
  four covariant exchanges;  I^f = f-even part of I, and I^E' != Comp_E'.
  I^E' is not a Lie algebra: the bracket of two E'-even qubit identifications is E'-odd (a matching).
  the part of I^f that D sees, I^f cap D = 1 + (f-even single-qubit), closed under brackets? equal to Comp_f cap D?
    E (plain; Letter, Lean) : closed True; = Comp_f cap D True
    E' = E o T (F-CT-10)    : closed False; = Comp_f cap D False
    Fm = (-1)^Nq E'         : closed True; = Comp_f cap D True
    (-1)^NQ E'              : closed False; = Comp_f cap D False
    sigma E' = (-1)^N E'    : closed True; = Comp_f cap D True
Rules on D:
  f = E   D cap (I^f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  f = E   D cap (Comp_f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  f = E'  D cap (I^f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  f = E'  D cap (Comp_f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 0) + 3 outside, = R_f: False; 1/value 139.712643 (M_L), 138.347888 (word rule)
  f = Fm  D cap (I^f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  f = Fm  D cap (Comp_f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  f = FQ  D cap (I^f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  f = FQ  D cap (Comp_f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 0) + 3 outside, = R_f: False; 1/value 139.712643 (M_L), 138.347888 (word rule)
  f = sE' D cap (I^f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  f = sE' D cap (Comp_f)^perp: dim 172, classes (79, 48, 42, 3), = R_f: True; 1/value 137.035999 (M_L), 137.035999 (word rule)
  D cap stab_Omega^perp = P2 + C+ (every frame); P<=2 cap stab_Omega^perp has dim 180 (D is needed).
  two-clause covariant form for E': R_E' = P2 + (D_0 cap stab_Omega) = D_0 cap (P2 + Lie(G_Omega)).
Exchanges on P<=2: G_Omega-covariance (f ad_K = ad_K f, 11 generators), involution, algebra type on two letters:
  E (plain; Letter, Lean) : covariant False; involution True; automorphism
  E' = E o T (F-CT-10)    : covariant True; involution True; anti-automorphism
  Fm = (-1)^Nq E'         : covariant True; involution True; neither
  (-1)^NQ E'              : covariant True; involution True; neither
  sigma E' = (-1)^N E'    : covariant True; involution True; neither
  Schur: the G_Omega-intertwiners V_q1 -> V_q2 and V_Q1 -> V_Q2 are lines (b -> b^T), so the covariant
  letter-wise exchanges are (eps_Q)^NQ (eps_q)^Nq E'; only E' is an (anti-)automorphism of B(H).
  readers remark: -b^T = sigma_y b sigma_y on qubit letters, and Fm = Ad_W, W = (sigma_y (x) sigma_y) SWAP_q, on all
  16 basis operators of P<=2 without qutrit letters: Fm identifies the read qubits by the matching that undoes
  the conjugation; at the qutrit copies the only intertwiner is the transpose (no unitary does it).
  operator form, every frame: R_f = D_0 cap ker((1 + f)[N = 1]); the occupation projector [N = 1] is the clause.

6. Collapse X -> X|Omega> under the transpose identity (Prop. 8)
----------------------------------------------------------------
rank kappa on P<=2: 36 (of 36);  ker kappa cap P<=1 = Lie(G_Omega) (11);  kappa(C) = 0;
kappa(C+) = kappa(E'-odd qq products), dim 3, inside kappa(P2);  plain frame: dim kappa(C_L) = 1, dim kappa(C_L+) = 2;
P2 + (D_0 cap ker kappa) = D_0.

